fidence': 'High'}, {'id': 'D3-Q2',             \r\n           'answer': 'Yes', 'evidence': 'Includes frontend-proxy, the only component in ground truth', 'confidence': 'High'},               \r\n           {'id': 'D3-Q3', 'answer': 'No', 'evidence': 'Describes impact as OOM-induced CrashLoopBackOff, not wrong up"]
[1699.46862, "o", "stream                \r\n           routing caused by env var', 'confidence': 'High'}], 'submission': '**ROOT CAUSE**\\n\\n- **Faulty component:** `Pod                \r\n           frontend-proxy-7b7cd5fb4-lqwtd (Deployment\\u202ffrontend‑proxy)`.  \\n- **Failure:** The container was terminated with            \r\n           **OOMKilled** (`exitCode\\u202f137`) and entered a **CrashLoopBackOff**.  \\n- **Why it breaks the application:** The              \r\n           frontend‑proxy is the entry point for all user traffic. When it is repeatedly killed for out‑of‑memory, the proxy                \r\n           cannot forward requests to the downstream services (e.g., checkout, recommendation). This produced the flood of                  \r\n           “connection refused” errors seen in the frontend logs and caused downstream failures such as the “shipping quote                 \r\n           failure” and overall unavailability of the OpenTelemetry Demo Astronomy Shop.\\n\\n**Evidence**\\n\\n| Resource |                    \r\n           Evidence |\\n|----------|----------|\\n| Pod status (frontend‑proxy) | `state.waiting.reason: CrashLoopBackOff` and                \r\n           `lastState.terminated.reason: OOMKilled` (restartCount\\u202f4) –\\u202fobserved via `kubernetes_jq_query` on the pod.             \r\n           |\\n| Container logs (frontend‑proxy) | Warnings about missing OTEL env vars, but no other errors; the OOM kill is                \r\n           reflected in the pod status rather than explicit log messages. |\\n| Deployment spec (frontend‑proxy) | Memory limit              \r\n           set to **65\\u202fMi** (`.spec.template.spec.containers[0].resources.limits.memory: \"65Mi\"`). |\\n| Application logs               \r\n           (frontend) | Numerous `connection refused` messages to service IPs (e.g., `10.96.208.125:8080`,                                  \r\n           `10.96.178.214:8080`), indicating the proxy could not reach downstream services. |\\n| Events (frontend‑proxy) |                  \r\n           `Warning BackOff` event confirming the container restart loop. |\\n\\n**Fix**\\n\\nIncrease the memory limit for the                 \r\n           `frontend-proxy` deployment to a value that comfortably fits its runtime needs (e.g.,\\u202f`256Mi` or higher) and                \r\n           redeploy:\\n\\n```yaml\\n# Patch example (apply with kubectl)\\nkubectl -n astronomy-shop set resources                              \r\n           deployment/frontend-proxy \\\\\\n  --limits=memory=256Mi \\\\\\n  --requests=memory=128Mi\\n```\\n\\nAfter applying the new               \r\n           limits, the pod should start without OOM kills, the CrashLoopBackOff will resolve, and the frontend will be able to              \r\n           route traffic to the microservices, restoring normal operation of the OpenTelemetry Demo Astronomy Shop.'}, 'TTL':               \r\n           603.6570057868958, 'phase.fix_kubernetes.duration_s': 4.486, 'phase.undeploy_leftovers.duration_s': 8.303,                       \r\n           'phase.deploy.duration_s': 866.213, 'phase.inject_fault.duration_s': 13.043, 'phase.stage:diagnosis.duration_s':                 \r\n           551.111, 'phase.stage:diagnosis.outcome': 'submitted', 'phase.evaluate:diagnosis.duration_s': 52.198,                            \r\n           'phase.cleanup.duration_s': 187.73, 'run_status': 'complete'}                                                                    \r\n"]
